  "design": "Error versus training-set size at 128 / 512 / 2048 / 4608 cases for all three families, using each family PUBLISHED reference configuration unchanged so that the ONLY thing varying across a ladder is the number of training cases (DESIGN 5.3). Every rung draws from the same cheap-fidelity bank, so fidelity is constant along a ladder. unet-pinned128 is control G2: the same configuration, the same budget and the same 128 physical cases at the PINNED 4096 reference fidelity, which measures the target-fidelity effect at fixed data size. unet-n4608-long triples the wall at the top rung to test whether the budget binds there. Equal 3000 s wall per rung -- the PUBLISHED per-arm budget, so the n=128 rung is directly comparable to the published arms as well as to its own ladder; at fixed batch size that is very nearly equal optimisation steps, so a rung differs from its neighbours in the data the same number of gradient steps is drawn from.",
